<p class="MsoNormal text-align-justify">The complete circuit diagram for the <strong>IoT Based Automated Inventory Management System</strong> is shown below.</p>

<p class="MsoNormal text-align-justify"><img alt="Automatic Inventory Management System Circuit Diagram" data-entity-type="file" data-entity-uuid="78946f8d-1739-4827-8af7-56078a10ab47" src="/sites/default/files/inline-images/Automatic-Inventory-Management-Schematic.png" /></p>

<p class="MsoNormal text-align-justify">The circuit diagram of inventory is very simple. Here, we connected the OLED display to the I2C pins of NodeMCU, which are the D1 and D2 pins on the board. Next, we connect the loadcell to NodeMCU. Loadcell has four wires - Red, Black, Green, and White. The color may vary according to the manufacturers, so it's better to refer to the <strong>datasheet</strong>. Connect red to E+ of HX711 board, connect black to E-, connect white to A+, and connect green to A-, Dout, and clock of the board connect to D5 and D6,&nbsp;respectively. Then connect&nbsp;the grounds of the OLED display and amplifier to the ground of NodeMCU. OLED and the load cell amplifier work on 5v, but the NodeMCU doesn't have 5v pins so we have to use a 5v regulator with the circuit. The image given below shows the breadboard prototype.</p>

